1
00:00:01,080 --> 00:00:02,280
Reading Task

2
00:00:04,480 --> 00:00:06,980
The Open Hand, a Universal Sign

3
00:00:08,820 --> 00:00:13,880
When meeting people at the airport, most people smile and shake hands with people they meet.

4
00:00:14,820 --> 00:00:18,540
We know that a smile is usually a sign that people feel friendly

5
00:00:18,540 --> 00:00:22,660
and happy, but what if we don't know who the new person is?

6
00:00:23,840 --> 00:00:26,020
What if we are not introduced by a friend?

7
00:00:26,020 --> 00:00:30,420
What if we are meeting a stranger in an unfamiliar place?

8
00:00:31,640 --> 00:00:35,900
Sometimes people are dangerous and humans have to find ways to protect themselves.

9
00:00:36,660 --> 00:00:39,540
We have to make sure we can trust people we do not know,

10
00:00:39,980 --> 00:00:42,080
and we have to show that we are not dangerous.

11
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:45,680
Showing Our hands means that we are not armed.

12
00:00:46,920 --> 00:00:51,320
In many cultures today, the Western custom of shaking hands is used.

13
00:00:52,260 --> 00:00:56,740
We use our right hand, which is usually stronger than the left one.

14
00:00:57,900 --> 00:00:59,700
If we are using our hand this way,

15
00:00:59,820 --> 00:01:02,260
it cannot be holding a knife or a gun.

16
00:01:03,100 --> 00:01:05,120
It shows that we trust the other person,

17
00:01:05,120 --> 00:01:08,120
and that the other person can trust us.

18
00:01:10,520 --> 00:01:12,460
Not all cultures use the handshake,

19
00:01:12,480 --> 00:01:17,120
and people in many Asian cultures do not always touch another person.

20
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:21,300
The traditional greeting in China was to cover the left hand

21
00:01:21,300 --> 00:01:22,620
with the right and bow.

22
00:01:32,760 --> 00:01:36,860
In India, Hindu people join their hands in front of their faces

23
00:01:36,860 --> 00:01:38,720
and bow their heads.

24
00:01:40,540 --> 00:01:45,380
A Muslim will touch his heart, mouth and forehead(额) to show respect.

25
00:01:46,200 --> 00:01:50,060
Even young people in the West now give each other the "high five",

26
00:01:50,060 --> 00:01:53,220
when they slap(拍) each other's hands high in the air.

27
00:01:53,920 --> 00:01:55,720
They are all keeping their hands busy.

28
00:01:56,320 --> 00:02:00,440
In almost all cultures, to smile and show an open right hand means, "

29
00:02:00,720 --> 00:02:02,620
Welcome, you are safe with me.
